From: theycallmeboxy <82409831+theycallmeboxy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 20:59:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] panvk/csf: skip IDVS index buffer and VARY_SIZE writes that
 repeat the held values

Every draw wrote VARY_SIZE, and every indexed draw INDEX_BUFFER_SIZE and
INDEX_BUFFER (a MOVE32 and a MOVE48), although they change only with the
raster VS variant and with vkCmdBindIndexBuffer. That is 3 of the about 13
vertex/tiler instructions of a typical DXVK indexed draw that only changed
descriptors, each paid in cs_move*_to, the CS allocation and the CSF
front end.

Nothing but prepare_draw() writes these three registers, so remember the
values last written at the top level of the CS and skip a write of the same
value. The cache is per command buffer and cleared wherever the register
state becomes unknown: command buffer reset/begin and the state reset after
vkCmdExecuteCommands (both clear the graphics state), and CS segment cuts,
through gfx_state_set_all_dirty(). Draws that may be recorded inside CS loops
or conditionals never use it and leave it cleared: gpu_prerast generated
draws, indirect draws, and anything recorded while a CS block is open. The
values are compared, not inferred from dirty bits, so a variant change that
sets no dirty bit can't leave a stale VARY_SIZE.

The launch registers (GLOBAL_ATTRIBUTE_OFFSET, INSTANCE_*) are left alone:
indirect and gpu_prerast paths load or patch them from the GPU.

PANVK_NO_IDVS_REG_CACHE=1 writes the registers on every draw again.

Effect on the CS: 1 instruction less per draw, 3 per indexed draw that keeps
its index buffer (DXVK draws usually do).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
