Purpose: D2: CPU/CS per draw: skip INDEX_BUFFER, INDEX_BUFFER_SIZE and VARY_SIZE writes that repeat the values the registers already hold (value cache for top-level plain draws, cleared wherever register state becomes unknown; indirect, gpu_prerast and in-CS-block draws always write); 1 CS instruction less per draw, 3 per indexed draw that keeps its index buffer. PANVK_NO_IDVS_REG_CACHE=1 reverts
Upstream-commit: none
Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC6 (Anbernic RG477M, Dimensity 8300, v11)
Tested Kbase UAPI: CSF 1.21 / MediaTek
Dependencies: none; applies on the full g615-v11-csf series after rg477m/023
Validation test: draw-path batch rg477m/023-027 on the device (drawcpu bench, DXVK pattern, 20,000 draws x 20 reps, pinned A715 at max clock, 10 interleaved runs per build): 543.6 -> 467.9 ns per recorded draw (-14%); with rg477m/024, 025 and 027 switched off (PANVK_NO_IDVS_REG_CACHE=1 PANVK_NO_SYSVAL_GATE=1 PANVK_NO_DESC_SPLIT=1) 501.8, so the three together about -7%; PanProbe 38/38 x2; Arkham Asylum (CPU-bound DXVK, quietd Stock, 10 interleaved rounds + 3) gameplay fps unchanged (median 36.4 base vs 36.55), launch failures 0/13 base vs 2/13 (known B5 signatures, Fisher p~0.48, n.s.); combined build next.so (15c3385bbe40, rg477m/023-037): PanProbe 38/38 x2 (unsafe profile 37/38, only the bc_decode raw readback, by design); 16-game boot sweep 2026-10-25 in quietd Stock mode: Hades 60, Jupiter Hell 59, Risk of Rain 2 38, Moonlighter 60, Megabonk 60, Portal 2 60, Gladius 60, Crysis 3 Remastered 60 fps; Arkham Asylum to the menu; Factorio and Ashes menus render as before; Descenders, Tomb Raider, Doom 3 BFG and Metro 2033 match their known states; 0 GPU faults; Serious Sam bot benchmark A-B-B-A compat 49.2/52.7 vs next 53.3/51.1 fps; Arkham Asylum 20-round interleaved A/B 2026-10-25 (quietd Stock), base rg477m vs next: launch failures 1/20 vs 0/20 (session total 1/33 vs 4/36, not significant; B5 signatures also seen on the stock driver), gameplay fps median 36.4 vs 36.5, speckcount on 3 gameplay frames per run 0-1 px in both arms (base 2 runs with 1 px, next 3 runs with 1 px; the old specks bug gave tens to hundreds): no specks
